BEFORE YOU DISTRIBUTE (TEMPLATE USERS READ THIS)
================================================================================

Shipping a Tauri app is a binary distribution. Your installers statically link
every Rust crate in src-tauri/Cargo.lock and bundle the compiled frontend, so
the notice requirements of those licenses apply to you, not just to this
template. MIT and BSD require the copyright notice and permission text to
travel with binary distributions; Apache-2.0 additionally requires that you
carry any NOTICE file from the upstream project.

Do not hand-maintain that list, and do not assume this file covers it — it
does not. Generate it from your own lockfiles:

  Rust      cargo install cargo-about
            cargo about generate about.hbs > licenses.html
            (run from src-tauri/)

  npm       pnpm dlx license-checker-rseidelsohn --production --plainVertical

Tauri itself is dual-licensed Apache-2.0 OR MIT; the wider crate ecosystem is
predominantly the same dual license, with a handful of exceptions that the
tooling above will surface. Review the generated output for anything copyleft
before you ship.

If you keep this file in your own project, replace this section with the notice
you generated, and update the vendored-source section above to match whatever
you actually vendor.
